    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "title": "Delivered from the shackles of stress",
      "description": "IHD programme champions mental well-being among community health promoters",
      "date": "Nov 05, 2025",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Maureen Ooko",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "92-Banner.png"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "On a hot afternoon in an urban informal settlement in Nairobi, we meet Joyce, not her real name, a Community Health Promoter (CHP) who narrates the difficult circumstances in which she performs her tasks."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "As a CHP, she has a clear mission: check in on families, share health information, and guide them on where to seek care when needed. However, often, what awaits her is not a warm welcome."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"In some households, people are angry or stressed and take it out on me. They do not want to talk, and sometimes they are very rude.\" she says."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For Joyce, who supports 100 households including her own, the emotional toll is heavy. A single bad encounter can put her in a sour mood the entire day."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"When one of the household members shouts at me, I leave feeling angry. I carry that weight home, and unfortunately, my family feels it too.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At home, small inconveniences often trigger an overreaction."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " \"When my child misbehaves, all the bottled-up anger from the day comes out and I punish her more harshly than I should. It is not fair to her,\" she adds."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A new beginning",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "One day, her supervisor informed her and her colleagues of a mental well-being and resilience training programme offered by the Aga Khan University Institute for Human Development (IHD) with support from the Johnson & Johnson Foundation."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The programme comprised of two interventions - a mental health literacy programme and the World Health Organization (WHO) developed Self Help Plus (SH+) course. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The mental health literacy programme incorporated modules to raise mental health awareness, challenge stigma, promote early help-seeking behaviour and encourage positive coping strategies. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The SH+ course is a 5-session stress management course for adults who experience stressful conditions. It has been shown to reduce psychological distress and prevent the onset of mental disorders."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For the first time, CHPs like her, often the first point of contact for health issues in the community, were being offered tools to care for their own mental well-being. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"I signed up immediately,\" Joyce says, her eyes gleaming with joy. \"We always help others, but no one ever asks about our mental health. This was our chance to get the support we needed.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Through the training, Joyce learnt practical ways to manage stress, ease tense situations, and handle her emotions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"I learnt how to react to people when they are angry or in a bad mood. Now, when someone seems stressed or upset, I probe further and try to find out what is wrong. It has completely changed how I relate to households.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Families who once shut her out now welcome her visits. Conversations flow easily, her work feels more fulfilling, and she reaches more people."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " At home, the transformation was just as powerful."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"I no longer shout when I am upset. I take time to talk to my child and show her love. Our home feels peaceful now and my child talks to me openly because she knows I will listen.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Championing mental health in the community",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The training not only changed Joyce's personal life but also shifted how she views mental health in her community."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"Before, I feared people with mental health disorders. I avoided them,\" she admits. \"But now I know they need help, not isolation.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Armed with new knowledge, Joyce and her fellow CHPs are now sensitising the community about mental health. They are encouraging people to support rather than shun those in distress."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"Sometimes you find that a person is not suffering from a mental illness but rather the person is stressed. People need someone to talk to, someone who understands,\" she adds."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Through the programme, over 600 healthcare workers in Nairobi County including community health promoters, nurses, clinical officers, medical officers, laboratory and pharmacy personnel have been trained to better care for their own mental well-being and guide others to seek help when needed. "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
